    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d422">

                <pb facs="0398" n="324" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg324"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr. Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 162.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 5, 1865,</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Tour despatch No. 91, of the 11th ultimo,
                    with its accompanying copy of a note which you addressed to Mr. Drouyu de Lhuys,
                    relative to the policy of France in according to the insurgents belligerent
                    rights, has been received, and, in reply, I have to inform you that the manner
                    in which you treated the subject in your communication is approved.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bigelow,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
